body:
## Describe the bug

We're self-hosting Supabase. I'm getting "JWS Invalid Signature" error on requests made through an admin client instance. Service key is valid, we are using that same key with the GoTrue library in our GO server.

## To Reproduce

```
const supabaseAdmin = createClient(
	supabaseUrl,
	supabaseServiceKey,
	{
		auth: {
			autoRefreshToken: false,
			persistSession: false
		}
	}
)
const { data, error } = await supabaseAdmin.from("some_table").select("*").limit(50)
```

That results in this error:
```
{
  code: 'PGRST301',
  details: null,
  hint: null,
  message: 'JWSError JWSInvalidSignature'
}
```

Any idea why this happens? It wasn't happening with the hosted version.
